    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 the most dangerous class of bugs in distributed systems, where requests complete successfully but with degraded quality, incorrect outputs, or unmeasured performance regressions.\n\n**How to use this checklist:** Each item should be executed and explicitly marked PASS/FAIL/SKIPPED with evidence attached. \"SKIPPED\" items require a written justification. A system is not validated until every item has a disposition.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical system.\n\n### 1.1 Model and Weights\n- [ ] **Model hash verification.** Compute and compare a cryptographic hash (SHA-256) of the model weights on every node. Do not rely on file paths, filenames, or timestamps \u2014 these are frequently identical across divergent weights (e.g., a partially-written checkpoint that was later overwritten).\n- [ ] **Checkpoint load completeness.** Verify that sharded weights were fully loaded \u2014 not just that loading \"succeeded.\" Check for:\n  - Missing shards silently initialized to random values (a classic silent failure)\n  - Dtype mismatches (e.g., one node loading fp16, another bf16)\n  - Quantization config identity (same quantization scheme, group size, calibration data hash on all nodes)\n- [ ] **Tokenizer identity.** Hash the tokenizer files (vocab, merges, special tokens) on all nodes. Tokenizer drift between nodes causes subtle quality degradation that is very hard to diagnose later.\n- [ ] **Generation config identity.** Sampling parameters, default temperature, top-p, stop sequences, and max context length must be identical everywhere.\n\n### 1.2 Runtime",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
